%% Topic 5 answers — examiner's-eye box; included by T5QA and the compiled QA volume.

::: eye | Topic 5 is won with current, dated data
Every question on this topic is about Pakistan **now**, so the examiner rewards **dated figures with sources**: MMR ==186== (PMMS 2019), female literacy about ==53%== (Census 2023), female labour-force participation ==24.4%== (LFS 2024–25), Global Gender Gap ==148/148== (2025) and ==143/145== (2026), the mobile-internet gap ==38% → 25%== (GSMA). Notice how the same small set of numbers and laws — Articles 25 and 34, MFLO 1961, the 2006 Act, the Harassment Act 2010, the 2016 honour law, the LHW Programme — is re-cut for each question. The two health questions of 2017 and 2023 overlap; they are answered separately to show how "within available resources" and "status as a whole" change the answer.
:::
